    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms all main sources \u2014 including the regenerated OpenAPI DTOs \u2014 compiled).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter so it's persisted and returned.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the others kept in sync).\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, compute and set the code at creation time via a new `nextCustomerCode` helper: `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", findAllOwners().size() + 1)` (one more than the current owner count). It's persisted so the value is stable and reflects creation-order \u2014 e.g. `smithers` \u2192 `SMI-000N`, `jones` \u2192 `JON-000(N+1)`.\n\nThe code is fixed at creation (not recomputed on read), which is what makes the test's `cb == ca + 1` invariant hold.",
